# Where a hash leaves its packed encoding — 512 fields, 64-byte fields and values (Redis 7.2's
# defaults, research D-20) — and that it never comes back. A packed hash answers in insertion order in
# both servers, so it is compared exactly; a converted one answers in table order in both, so [pairs].
# An exact line at 512 fields holds kesh to the same boundary: converting early would reorder it.
